{"name":"Cypress Vine","hex":"#5e6552","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cypress vine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tropical morning glory of species Ipomoea quamoclit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cypress_vine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ipomoea quamoclit","blocks":[{"text":"Ipomoea quamoclit, commonly known as cypress vine, cypress vine morning glory, cardinal creeper, cardinal vine, star glory, star of Bethlehem or hummingbird vine, is a species of vine in the family Convolvulaceae native to tropical regions of the Americas and naturalized elsewhere in the tropics."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Cyprus_vine_flower.jpg/330px-Cyprus_vine_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipomoea_quamoclit"},{"title":"Cypress","blocks":[{"text":"Cypress is a common name for species in several genera in the family Cupressaceae. They grow in temperate climates and subtropical regions of Asia, Europe, and North America."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cypress"},{"title":"Vine","blocks":[{"text":"A vine is any plant with a growth habit of trailing or scandent stems, lianas, or runners. The word vine can also refer to such stems or runners themselves, for instance, when used in wicker work."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg/330px-%22A_Momordica_charantia-_bitter_guard_plant%22.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vine"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Ipomoea_Quamoclit.jpg/120px-Ipomoea_Quamoclit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Ipomoea_Quamoclit.jpg/250px-Ipomoea_Quamoclit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped